WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.400
 This is my perfect lasagna.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.780
Start by finely chopping onion, carrots, and celery.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.580
Add the mirepoix to a large pot with butter and oil, and sauté.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.650
Add in the seasonings and follow with tomato paste

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.290
stirring constantly, until you see it darken in color.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.220
The sugars will caramelize, adding richness and reducing acidity.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.160
Next, add ground beef, ground pork, and pancetta

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.210
and allow the heat to reduce the sugars and proteins, browning our meat.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.450
This is known as the maillard reaction.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.020
Add milk, wine, and bring to a simmer, and add some oregano.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.740
Now, for the ricotta béchamel.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.200
Start with butter in a pan over medium-low heat.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.180
Stir in the flour and whisk constantly for one minute.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.340
The process of combining fat and flour creates a thickening agent for our sauce.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.960
Now, add the milk and bring to a simmer.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.580
Stir in the salt and nutmeg and let cool before folding in the ricotta cheese.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:04.480
Slice three al dente noodles lengthwise to help fit the pan, and let's assemble.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:10.520
Start with the béchamel, then noodles. Add another layer of ricotta béchamel, then the bolognese.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.990
Add some parmesan cheese and top with one more layer of noodles.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:14.770
And repeat.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.800
Top with a final layer of béchamel, parmesan, and mozzarella.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.220
Bake this uncovered for 40 minutes.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.230
And wow, look at that.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:25.940
Almost perfect.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.600
So, what makes it perfect?

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.930
Well, the best thing about lasagna is that it can be built however you want.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.130
Perfect is in the eye of the beholder.

